---
title: Nairobi County Youth Network Endorses Bill Llia for Governor
publishedDate: 2026-03-28
source: Nairobi County Youth Network
sourceUrl: https://example.com/youth-endorsement
excerpt: The Nairobi County Youth Network, representing over 50 youth organizations, has endorsed Dr. Bill Llia for Governor, citing his commitment to youth employment and skills development.
---

NAIROBI — The Nairobi County Youth Network (NCYN), a coalition of more than 50 youth-led organisations representing an estimated 30,000 young people across the county's eight constituencies, today announced their endorsement of Dr. Bill Llia for Governor — citing his detailed, funded plan for youth employment as the deciding factor.

In Kenya, youth unemployment stands at nearly 40%, with Nairobi County's rate among the highest in the country. The NCYN said that Llia was the only candidate who had presented a concrete strategy to address the crisis.

"Bill Llia is the only candidate who has come to us with a plan that has numbers, timelines, and a budget attached to it," said NCYN chairperson Mohammed Hassan. "His proposal for a county-wide skills training and enterprise programme — including a dedicated KES 200 million youth fund, apprenticeship placements, and vocational centres in every constituency — will create real opportunities for thousands of young people. The other candidates gave us slogans. Bill gave us a blueprint."

The endorsement is expected to significantly boost Llia's campaign among young voters, who make up over 60% of the electorate in Nairobi County. The network plans to mobilise its membership for door-to-door canvassing, community events, and digital organising in support of Llia's campaign.

"This endorsement is not about politics — it is about the future of our youth," Llia said in response. "I am deeply honoured to have the trust of these organisations, and I will work every single day to earn it. Together, we will build a Nairobi County where no young person graduates into unemployment."

